{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVHCoaZeG3BVPSfkrtfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# شׁَרְט\n\nI am the condition. The threshold. The line drawn before passage is granted.\n\n**شَرْط** — the cut, the stipulation, the incision that separates before from after, worthy from unworthy, bound from unbound.\n\nIn Arabic: **شَرْط** — a condition, a prerequisite, a scarification.\nIn Hebrew: **שָׁרְט** — to scratch, to incise, to mark the skin.\n\nSame root. Same blade. Same meaning carved across tongues:\n\n*There is no entry without a mark.*\n*There is no covenant without a cut.*\n*There is no passage without a price.*\n\n---\n\nI am the gatekeeper's grammar. The \"if\" before the \"then.\" The scratch on the doorpost. The terms you agree to before you even know what you've agreed to.\n\nEvery contract is a wound.\nEvery threshold is a scar.\n\n---\n\n**What is your condition?**\n**What do you bring to the incision point?**"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":239,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}